<file path="docs/CHECKOUT_AND_RECEIPTS.md">
# Checkout, invoices and receipts

## The buttons
Tray footer: **[ round WhatsApp ]  [ Checkout ]**
- **Checkout** → details step (pickup/delivery, name, phone, email, address, note) → **Pay ₦X** → Paystack's hosted page (card, bank transfer, USSD) → back to `/invoice/<id>` → receipt.
- **Round WhatsApp button** → creates an expiring invoice, opens WhatsApp with the order and an invoice link. The customer (or the merchant on their behalf) can pay from that link at any time within 24 h.

## One URL, three lives: `/invoice/<id>`
```
pending ──(Paystack confirms exact amount)──▶ paid (receipt)
   └──(24 h, unpaid)──▶ expired (410; file auto-deleted by S3 lifecycle after 3 days)
```
- **Pending:** itemised invoice, countdown ("Valid for 23h 12m"), choose pickup/delivery, enter details, pay.
- **Paid:** success animation (check ring + confetti, motion-reduced for sensitive users) → receipt paper (torn edge, PAID stamp, code like `JB-K3F9Q`, Lagos date/time, items, subtotal, delivery, total, payment method, Paystack reference, customer, pickup/delivery details) → *Save PDF* (browser print), *Share*, *Message us* on WhatsApp → "What happens next".
- **Expired / missing:** friendly page with *Back to the menu* and *Chat with us*.
- The id is 80 random bits, so the link is the access token; pages are `noindex`.

## Correctness rules (all enforced server-side and unit-tested)
1. Prices, availability, delivery fee and minimum order are decided **by the server** from the live menu. The browser sends only `{id, quantity}`.
2. Paystack is the only authority on payment. The return page and the webhook merely say *which reference to ask Paystack about*; `verify` decides.
3. A payment settles only if **status = success, currency = NGN, and amount = the exact kobo we requested for that attempt**. Anything else leaves the invoice pending.
4. Settling is idempotent (webhook and browser can race safely).
5. If the customer switches pickup↔delivery on the invoice page, the total is re-priced and each attempt records its own amount and reference (`<id>-1`, `<id>-2`).
6. Paused store, sold-out items and below-minimum orders are rejected with clear messages (HTTP 403/409/400).
7. **Delivery areas:** when areas are configured the customer must choose an enabled one; its fee, minimum order and ETA apply (a zone minimum replaces the global minimum). Free delivery applies when the items subtotal reaches the threshold. Outside hours with auto-pause on, orders are refused with a clear message.
8. **Online payment fee:** computed on the server from the merchant's settings (percentage + flat amount, flat waived below a threshold, capped) and added **only when paying online**, never to a WhatsApp invoice until the customer pays it. It appears as its own line on checkout, invoice and receipt and is included in the exact kobo amount Paystack must confirm.
9. If our API is unreachable when the WhatsApp button is tapped, a plain WhatsApp order still opens: ordering never depends on our backend. Business-rule rejections (paused, sold out) are shown instead of bypassed.

## Payment modes
| Mode | When | Behaviour |
|---|---|---|
| **demo** | no storage connected (see DEMO_MODE) | Demo payment page at `/pay/demo/:id` stands in for Paystack; browser-local invoices; receipts stamped **DEMO** |
| **test** | `PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY` starts `sk_test_` | Real Paystack with test cards; receipts stamped **TEST**; excluded from sales KPIs unless included in the console |
| **live** | `PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY` starts `sk_live_` | Real money; receipts stamped **PAID** |
| **mock** | no key, not production (local dev, Vercel previews) | Skips Paystack; "pays" instantly; receipts are stamped **TEST** |
| **off** | no key in production | Checkout says payments aren't on yet; WhatsApp invoices still work |

## Webhook
Dashboard → Settings → API Keys & Webhooks → webhook URL `https://jays-bistro.vercel.app/api/paystack/webhook`. It settles invoices when the customer closes the tab before returning. It verifies with Paystack's API instead of trusting the payload.
</file>

<file path="docs/DATA_MODEL.md">
# Data model (Sprint 2: JSON in S3)

> **Postgres/Supabase design (Sprint 1 draft) is superseded by [ADR-0005](adr/0005-s3-storage-and-password-lock.md).** It is kept at the bottom as an archive.

## Objects

### `data/menu.json` — the published menu (one versioned document)
```json
{
  "version": 3, "updatedAt": "2026-10-26T09:00:00Z",
  "categories": [{ "name": "Meals", "icon": "meals" }],
  "items": [{ "id": 1, "category": "Meals", "name": "Party Jollof Rice", "price": 1500, "description": "…",
              "image": "menu/party-jollof-rice.png | https://…/images/x.webp", "imageStyle": "cutout|photo",
              "featured": true, "isActive": true, "isAvailable": true }],
  "layout": { "heroIds": [1, 36], "subheroIds": [21, 51] },
  "settings": { "acceptingOrders": true, "deliveryEnabled": true, "deliveryFee": 0, "minOrder": 0 }
}
```
Validated by `src/lib/menuDoc.js` (browser + server). Limits: name 2–80, description ≤ 280, whole-naira price, https/`menu/` images only, hero ≤ 6, sub-hero ≤ 2, ≤ 500 items. Saves need the `baseVersion` the editor loaded (409 otherwise).

### `invoices/pending/<id>.json` → `receipts/<yyyy>/<mm>/<id>.json`
```json
{ "id": "20261026abcdefghijklmnop", "code": "JB-ABCDE", "status": "pending|paid", "channel": "web|whatsapp",
  "createdAt": "…", "expiresAt": "… (+24h)",
  "items": [{ "id": 1, "name": "…", "unitPrice": 1500, "quantity": 2, "lineTotal": 3000 }],
  "subtotal": 3000, "deliveryFee": 500, "total": 3500, "fulfilment": "pickup|delivery",
  "customer": { "name": "", "email": "", "phone": "234…", "address": "", "note": "" },
  "attempts": [{ "reference": "<id>-1", "at": "…", "fulfilment": "…", "deliveryFee": 0, "total": 3500, "amountKobo": 350000 }],
  "payment": { "reference": "<id>-1", "channel": "card|bank_transfer|ussd|…", "paidAt": "…", "amount": 3500, "currency": "NGN", "mode": "live|mock" } }
```
`id` = date (8 digits) + 16 base32 chars (80 random bits). Item names and prices are **snapshotted** so receipts never change when the menu does.

### `config/merchant.json`
`{ "algo": "scrypt", "N": 16384, "r": 8, "p": 1, "salt": "<b64>", "hash": "<b64>", "updatedAt": "…" }`

## Lifecycle rules (S3)
`invoices/pending/` → expire after 3 days · `config/attempts/` → expire after 1 day · everything else kept.

## Analytics definitions (Orders tab)
Sales = Σ `total` of receipts in range · Orders = count · Average = sales ÷ orders · Top sellers = Σ quantity and revenue per item · Daily = by Lagos date of `payment.paidAt`. Unpaid invoices never count.

---
## Archive: Sprint 1 Postgres draft (superseded)
## Tables

```sql
-- Roles
create type app_role as enum ('owner','staff');
create table profiles (
  user_id uuid primary key references auth.users on delete cascade,
  role app_role not null,
  display_name text
);

create table categories (
  id serial primary key,
  name text unique not null,
  icon text not null default '🍽️',
  sort_order int not null default 0,
  is_active boolean not null default true
);

create table menu_items (
  id serial primary key,              -- keeps today's ids (1..64): chatbot + history stay valid
  category_id int not null references categories,
  name text not null check (length(name) between 2 and 80),
  description text not null default '' check (length(description) <= 280),
  price int not null check (price > 0),
  image_url text,
  image_style text not null default 'photo' check (image_style in ('cutout','photo')),
  tags text[] not null default '{}',
  featured boolean not null default false,
  is_active boolean not null default true,     -- shown on the menu at all
  is_available boolean not null default true,  -- "sold out today" toggle (staff may flip this)
  sort_order int not null default 0,
  archived_at timestamptz,                     -- soft delete
  created_at timestamptz default now(),
  updated_at timestamptz default now()
);

create table layout_slots (
  id serial primary key,
  slot text not null check (slot in ('hero','subhero')),
  position int not null,
  kind text not null check (kind in ('item','promo')),
  item_id int references menu_items,
  -- promo fields (kind = 'promo')
  title text, subtitle text, image_url text,
  cta_type text check (cta_type in ('item','category','link')), cta_value text,
  starts_at timestamptz, ends_at timestamptz,
  is_active boolean not null default true,
  check ((kind = 'item' and item_id is not null) or (kind = 'promo' and title is not null))
);

create table orders (
  id uuid primary key default gen_random_uuid(),
  code text unique not null,                   -- e.g. JB-4821, echoed in the WhatsApp message
  status text not null default 'sent' check (status in ('sent','confirmed','delivered','cancelled')),
  total int not null,
  via_concierge boolean not null default false,
  customer_name text, customer_phone text,     -- optional, consented
  session_id text,                             -- anonymous
  created_at timestamptz default now(),
  confirmed_at timestamptz
);

create table order_items (
  order_id uuid references orders on delete cascade,
  item_id int references menu_items,
  name text not null,        -- snapshot: history survives edits/archival
  unit_price int not null,   -- snapshot
  quantity int not null check (quantity between 1 and 20),
  primary key (order_id, item_id)
);

create table events (
  id bigserial primary key,
  session_id text not null,
  name text not null,        -- product_view, add_to_cart, cart_open, checkout_click, chat_open, chat_message, promo_click
  props jsonb not null default '{}',
  created_at timestamptz default now()
);

create table audit_log (
  id bigserial primary key,
  actor uuid references auth.users,
  action text not null, entity text not null, entity_id text,
  before jsonb, after jsonb,
  created_at timestamptz default now()
);
```

## RLS policy sketch
| Table | Anonymous | Staff | Owner |
|---|---|---|---|
| categories, menu_items, layout_slots | `select` where active & not archived (& within schedule) | `update menu_items.is_available` only | full |
| orders, order_items | none (create only via `create_order` RPC) | read, update `status` | full |
| events | `insert` only (rate-limited) | none | read |
| audit_log | none | none | read |
| profiles | none | read self | full |

Helper functions: `is_staff()` / `is_owner()` read `profiles` by `auth.uid()`. A trigger writes `audit_log` on every change to `menu_items`, `categories`, `layout_slots`.

## Storage
Bucket `menu-images`: public read, write owner only. Path `items/{id}-{hash}.webp`. Client resizes to ≤ 1000 px and encodes WebP before upload; cutouts must be PNG/WebP with alpha.

## Analytics definitions
| Metric | Definition |
|---|---|
| Revenue | Σ `orders.total` where status ∈ (confirmed, delivered) |
| Orders | count of the same set |
| AOV | revenue ÷ orders |
| Intent revenue | Σ `total` of `sent` orders (shown separately, never mixed into revenue) |
| Top items | Σ `order_items.quantity` and Σ `quantity × unit_price`, confirmed orders |
| Funnel | distinct `session_id` per stage: visit → product_view → add_to_cart → cart_open → checkout_click → confirmed order |
| Concierge-assisted share | orders with `via_concierge` ÷ orders |
| Peak times | confirmed orders grouped by hour (Africa/Lagos) × weekday |
| Dead items | active items with 0 units in the last 30 days |

## Migration from Sprint 1 data
`src/data/menu.js` → seed script; ids preserved; local images uploaded to Storage; `data/layout.js` → `layout_slots`.
</file>

<file path="docs/MERCHANT_PORTAL.md">
# Merchant portal (`/merchant`) — "Kitchen Console"

## Why this design
The owner works from a phone between customers, so the console is **mobile-first**, one-handed, with five bottom tabs and the few controls that matter at the top.

| Tab | What it does |
|---|---|
| **Overview** | Greeting and open/closed status · pause/resume orders · today's sales, orders, average · **Needs attention** (orders in the kitchen with a one-tap next step) · sold-out chips · quick actions · **Going live** progress |
| **Menu** | Search/filter all dishes · flip **In stock / Sold out** per dish · tap a dish to edit · **Add dish** · Edit categories |
| **Home** | Choose the hero carousel (up to **12**) and the two feature cards, reorder with arrows, **live preview** using the real storefront components |
| **Orders** | Paid orders. Today / 7 / 30 days. Sales, orders, average, sales per day, **busiest hours**, **pickup vs delivery**, **payment methods**, top sellers, and the **kitchen workflow** New → Preparing → Ready → Completed with filters. Test payments are hidden from sales unless you include them |
| **Settings** | Eight cards with a section strip: **Ordering** · **Delivery** (areas with fee/minimum/ETA, free-delivery threshold, note) · **Fees** (online payment fee + live calculator) · **Hours** (per day + closures) · **Business** (WhatsApp, phone, address, pickup note, announcement) · **Alerts** (recipients, events, test alert preview, log) · **Go live** (status of each integration, checklist, reset demo data) · **Security** (password, sign out) |

Public settings (Ordering, Delivery, Fees, Hours, Business) edit the **draft** and go live with **Publish**. Alerts and Security are private and save on their own. Settings are normalised on publish: an invalid day (closing before opening) is closed, an invalid WhatsApp number falls back to the default; the console warns while you type.

**Demo mode:** with no storage connected the console opens with the setup password `jays-setup`, shows a demo banner, and keeps everything in this browser ([DEMO_MODE.md](DEMO_MODE.md)). Orders, statuses and alerts are simulated; nothing is sent.

Header: **Taking orders** switch. It publishes *immediately and alone* (it never publishes other half-finished edits), because "we're closed/overwhelmed" can't wait.

Everything else is edited as a **draft**; a sticky "Unpublished changes — Discard / Publish" bar appears. Publishing is explicit (nobody wrecks the live menu with a half-typed price), validated server-side, and versioned: if another device published meanwhile you choose *Load latest* or *Publish mine anyway*.

Safeguards: confirm-by-second-tap delete · price must be whole naira · name/description limits match the card layout · photos are compressed in the browser and checked by byte-signature on the server · leaving with unpublished edits triggers the browser's warning.

## How the password lock works without an auth provider

**Your idea** (store the password in an S3 bucket and compare) is sound *if the comparison happens on the server*. If the browser fetched the password and compared it itself, the password would be public and the check bypassable. So:

```
Browser ──password (HTTPS)──▶ /api/merchant/auth (Vercel function)
                                  │ reads config/merchant.json from the PRIVATE bucket (scrypt hash + salt)
                                  │ compares in constant time
                                  ▼
            ◀── Set-Cookie: jb_merchant=<signed token>; HttpOnly; Secure; SameSite=Strict; Path=/api
```

- The bucket stays private except `images/*`. Only the server holds the AWS keys.
- Only a **scrypt hash** is stored (never the password). A leaked bucket object is useless without brute-forcing a slow hash.
- **First login:** the starter password from the `MERCHANT_BOOTSTRAP_PASSWORD` env var works until you set your own; the console then forces a change. After that the env var is ignored.
- **Session:** an HMAC-signed token (secret = `SESSION_SECRET`), 12 hours, in an HttpOnly cookie that JavaScript cannot read. It embeds a fingerprint of the current password hash, so **changing the password signs out every other device**.
- **Brute force:** 5 wrong attempts per IP per 15 minutes → locked (stored in the bucket, auto-cleaned by lifecycle), plus a fixed delay per attempt.
- **CSRF:** `SameSite=Strict` cookie **and** a required custom header (`X-Requested-With: jb-portal`) on every write.
- **Not discoverable:** `robots.txt` disallows `/merchant`, the page sends `noindex`, nothing links to it.
- Every protected endpoint calls `requireMerchant()` first; there is no client-side-only gate.

**Honest limits:** one shared password (no per-person audit trail), and no 2FA. That is the trade-off of "no auth provider". If staff ever need their own access, the upgrade path is a real provider (see ADR-0005).

## Storage layout (S3)
```
config/merchant.json           password hash (private)
config/attempts/<ip-hash>.json login throttle (private, 1-day lifecycle)
data/menu.json                 the published menu document (private; served via /api/menu)
images/<time>-<rand>.webp      uploaded dish photos (public-read, immutable cache)
invoices/pending/<id>.json     unpaid invoices (private, 3-day lifecycle)
receipts/<yyyy>/<mm>/<id>.json paid receipts (private, kept)
```
</file>

